WEBVTT

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:18.560
When Voltic Bicorn is destroyed, we both send

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.130
cards in our decks to our 
graveyards equal to its Level.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.060
Voltic Bicorn is Level 7!

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.700
Send seven cards in your 
deck to the graveyard!

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:34.360
Seven cards?

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.960
This strategy is...

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.790
Hey, he's...

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.150
Breo's strategy is to...

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.770
They finally noticed.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:51.240
I let End of the Storm be destroyed because 
I didn't need to leave it for Breo.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.580
Because Stardust Dragon 
isn't a threat to his deck.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.500
This is deck destruction!

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:22.130
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:27.670
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.140
Don't look back and keep going

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:37.940
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:42.910
There's no need to fear

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:50.590
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:56.590
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:01:57.330 --> 00:02:02.370
Streak to the infinite future

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:07.740
Dreams surpass their limits

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:15.880
And will lead you to a bright place

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:47.760
For the Team

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:55.150
The final hope for Team 5D's is Yusei Fudo!

00:02:55.140 --> 00:03:02.260
He managed to defeat Team Unicorn's Andore, 
but he took the second wheeler Breo's attack!

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:05.900
What will you do, Yusei Fudo?

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:09.680
Yusei, your hell is only starting!

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:12.140
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:16.440
If Breo's goal is to destroy his deck...

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:20.070
He'll use up Yusei's deck until 
there are zero cards left.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:23.230
Yusei won't be able to 
continue the duel and lose.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:26.120
And they still have Jean left.

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:32.800
In a team battle, deck destruction is a more 
effective strategy than eliminating life points.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:34.920
This is bad.

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:42.850
Master Atlas!

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.650
Take it easy, Jack!

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:48.300
What happened to the duel?

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.700
Yusei is currently battling 
the second player Breo.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:52.660
And Izayoi?

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:54.580
She lost against Andore.

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:57.770
To Andore?  That means...

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:03.390
Unless Yusei defeats Breo and Jean 
by himself, Team 5D's can't win.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.680
What's the status?

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:07.960
It's...

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:13.190
Breo's goal is deck destruction.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.830
There are 23 cards left in my deck.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.340
But for now...

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:20.290
My turn!

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:24.550
Good!  I can use this!

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.750
I activate Speed Spell - Accelerate Draw!

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:33.760
When I'm the only one with 12 Speed 
Counters, I draw two cards from my deck.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.670
He drew two cards?

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:39.690
Isn't it bad to draw more cards?

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:45.060
No.  Even if Yusei focuses on defense, 
Breo will keep executing his strategy.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:46.460
In that case...

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:51.470
You're planning to counterattack, 
but I've expected that, Yusei Fudo.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:56.630
My data says you'll try that to escape.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.200
Stardust Dragon attacks you directly!

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:08.880
I was waiting for that attack!

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.550
I activate my trap Regretful Tuning!

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:17.150
When I take a direct attack, I can Special 
Summon one Synchro Monster from my graveyard.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.650
Resurrect, Voltic Bicorn!

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:28.130
If the Special Summoned monster attacks, 
it's destroyed at the end of the Battle Phase.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:31.400
Voltic Bicorn resurrected again.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:34.590
If Voltic Bicorn is destroyed, both players

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:38.390
send seven cards in their 
decks to their graveyards.

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:42.550
Stardust and Voltic Bicorn have 
the same number of attack points.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:45.630
He's planning to destroy them both next turn

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:48.370
and use Voltic Bicorn's 
effect to destroy my deck.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.330
This kills two birds with one 
stone, just as Breo planned.

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:59.210
Yusei is perplexed, which will 
make his situation worse.

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.800
I set one card and end my turn.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:06.500
It's pointless, Yusei.  
I won't let you escape!

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:07.650
My turn!

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:12.890
Battle!  Voltic Bicorn 
attacks Stardust Dragon!

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:16.550
I won't let Stardust be destroyed!

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.110
I activate Synchro Striker Unit!

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:27.860
This card equips on to a Synchro Monster, and 
the equipped monster gains 1000 attack points!

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:34.720
I activate the trap card Flattery!

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:38.960
When your monster's attack 
points change during battle...

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:44.110
...my monster gains attack points equal 
to the change until the end of battle.

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:49.960
What?

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:51.660
Too bad, Yusei!

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:53.030
No way!

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:54.620
Stardust Dragon was...

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:59.940
Yusei increased its attack points, but he 
still caught up for mutual destruction.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.720
You can't escape from me!

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:09.140
Since Voltic Bicorn was destroyed, we both 
send seven cards in our decks to our graveyards!

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.280
I'm only getting started!

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:15.160
I activate the trap card Tuning Collapse!

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:15.600
What?

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:20.210
When your Synchro Monster 
is destroyed in battle, you

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:24.320
send cards in your deck to your 
graveyard equal to its Level.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:29.240
Since Stardust Dragon is 
Level 8, that's eight cards!

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:33.300
Since he already lost seven 
cards, that's 15 cards total.

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:34.860
No way!

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:41.050
Team Unicorn's Breo is incredible!

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:46.010
His deck destruction strategy using Voltic 
Bicorn and Tuning Collapse erupts!

00:07:46.010 --> 00:07:49.460
He instantly eliminated 
15 cards in Yusei's deck!

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:56.160
Not only did I lose the Stardust Dragon that Aki 
left for me, but I also lost 15 cards in my deck.

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:00.050
My deck...

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.300
...has five cards left.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:04.880
What can he do?

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:08.250
At this rate, Yusei and Team 5D's will lose!

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.430
And after Breo, they still have Jean!

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:17.900
Defeating two opponents with only 
five cards in his deck is impossible!

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:20.920
Your strategy is impressive, Jean.

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:23.620
No, it's not me.  It's Breo.

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:28.910
This strategy can't work without 
his extraordinary memory.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.660
That's true.

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:37.220
Breo memorizes and analyzes the opposing 
team's duel data to predict what they'll do.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:39.790
Then he defeats them by 
destroying their deck.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:45.900
Correct.  His memory is his dueling 
talent and most powerful weapon.

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:48.880
I can't replicate that skill.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:55.340
Andore's card-playing instincts 
and Breo's viable calculations.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:59.700
And Jean creates strategies for victory.

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:03.360
That's Team Unicorn.  That's our power.

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:07.800
This is how to battle as a team.

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:11.320
Instead of caring about my own victory, I can

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:15.830
unleash my full power if I 
focus on damaging my enemy.

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:20.560
Jean and Andore made me realize that.

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:28.570
As long as I can battle alongside them, 
I'll gladly be Team Unicorn's shield!

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:31.560
I set three cards and end my turn!

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:33.400
My turn!

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:37.360
There are four cards left in my deck.

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:39.490
I activate the Continuous 
Trap Tricolor Illusion!

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:46.070
As long as I have this 
card, you can't attack.

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:53.290
Once per turn, you draw a card, and you 
receive a different effect depending on that card.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:58.570
If you draw a spell card, 
add that card to your hand.

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:01.940
If it's a trap, you send that card and 
one card in your hand to the graveyard.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:06.710
If it's a monster, you add 
that card to your hand,

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:09.570
and you put one card in your 
hand on top of your deck.

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:17.330
However, you can send one card in your deck 
to your graveyard to destroy this card.

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:20.020
Yusei, what will you choose?

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:25.010
He doesn't want to send a card 
in his hand to his graveyard.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:29.060
I know that he's not the gambling type.

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:33.470
That means he'll definitely use that.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:38.500
Breo is going for it.

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:39.140
Yeah.

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:47.310
If Yusei uses Speed World 2's effect, 
he can destroy Tricolor Illusion.

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:52.090
But at that moment, the trap card 
Destruction Activator will activate.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:59.680
I can activate it when a spell or trap 
card destroys another card on my field.

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.730
Five cards in his deck will 
be sent to his graveyard!

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:11.220
I've memorized your deck data.  The 
probability that you'll draw a monster is 50%.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:13.180
Bring it, Yusei!

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:20.030
He looks completely confident, so he 
knows what I'm planning to do next.

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:21.880
If I continue on the same path...

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:30.100
If I'm going for it, now is the time!

00:11:30.510 --> 00:11:33.340
Due to Tricolor Illusion's 
effect, I draw a card!

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:37.550
He's taking Tricolor Illusion's effect?

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:39.750
He's gambling?

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:45.110
I drew a monster card!

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:49.950
Among his remaining four 
cards, he drew a monster!

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:52.550
I return one card in my hand to my deck.

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:54.330
I summon Junk Synchron!

00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:58.550
Synchro Summon?

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:04.960
Level 3 Junk Synchron tunes Level 2 
Card Breaker and Level 3 Dash Warrior!

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:13.740
Fighting vigor comes together to 
call forth the roaring spirit!

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:15.330
Become the path that lights the way!

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:19.010
Synchro Summon!

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:21.980
Pulverize, Junk Destroyer!

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:26.920
What?  Junk Destroyer?

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:31.220
When it's Synchro Summoned, 
I destroy a card on the

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:35.700
field for each of its non-Tuner 
Synchro Material Monsters!

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:37.610
Tidal Energy!

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:41.800
If this attack succeeds, Yusei wins!

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:43.500
Go, Yusei!

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:45.950
Junk Destroyer attacks you directly!

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:48.910
I refuse to lose!

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:51.240
I activate Damage Lance!

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:55.390
When a monster with 2000-or-more 
attack points attacks me directly...

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:59.450
...your monster loses 1000 attack points 
during battle, and you take 1000 points of damage!

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:09.170
Go!

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:11.310
Destroy Knuckle!

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:20.880
He did it!

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:22.220
Yusei won!

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.920
All right!  There's only one left!

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:28.070
But Yusei only has 1000 life points.

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:30.120
Even worse, he only has four 
cards left in his deck.

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:50.810
What kind of duelist is Jean?

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:54.050
He's Team Unicorn's leader.

00:13:54.210 --> 00:13:57.990
Jean probably formulates their strategies.

00:13:58.450 --> 00:14:01.960
Does that mean he's stronger 
than Andore and Breo?

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:10.220
Yusei, how will you fight him with 
only four cards in your deck?

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:15.610
Sorry, Jean.  I couldn't finish him.

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:21.230
Yusei also has natural 
card-playing instincts.

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:23.220
No, that's not all.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:29.710
I sense something more that can't 
be uncovered by analyzing data.

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:31.540
Something...

00:14:32.590 --> 00:14:37.140
He's the first opponent we've faced 
that fought this well against us.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:40.040
But he only has four cards in his deck.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:41.580
I will win.

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:44.560
That's my job.

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:50.960
It's time for Team Unicorn's 
last wheeler Jean!

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:55.040
Yusei Fudo has fought hard to defeat 
two members of Team Unicorn!

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:59.780
But he only has 1000 life points 
and four cards in his deck!

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:04.690
How will he overcome this crisis 
against the third assassin Jean?

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:11.380
Yusei Fudo, I'm impressed that 
you've forced me to duel.

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:14.360
Did you create this duel's strategies?

00:15:14.650 --> 00:15:15.820
That's right.

00:15:16.170 --> 00:15:22.300
Today's battle already started when 
Andore and I battled back then?

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:25.510
That's how team battle strategies work.

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:27.350
You're incredible.

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:36.840
I didn't know that team battles could be 
this complex and fun until I battled your team.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:40.690
I'm happy that I battled your team.

00:15:41.180 --> 00:15:44.980
Despite his predicament, 
Yusei Fudo is having fun.

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:50.420
Just as Breo said, there's something 
different about him than other duelists.

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:55.100
But I can't afford to lose.

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:58.830
Andore and Breo gave their 
all for the good of the team.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:03.640
We weren't strong duelists individually.

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:11.450
Command Knight attacks you directly!

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:19.360
I did it!  A huge come-from-behind victory!

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:21.340
I win!

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:25.190
Come back after you practice, kid genius!

00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:33.530
You're like another simple-minded guy I know.

00:16:33.710 --> 00:16:35.240
Why did you lose on purpose?

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:42.440
When you saw victory, you also saw your 
losing opponent's frustration and sadness.

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:44.370
Then you're no good.

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:48.210
You can't focus on winning, 
so you end up losing.

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:50.100
You don't know how I feel.

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:53.630
I do know because I'm the same.

00:16:55.370 --> 00:16:57.500
Want to battle together?

00:16:58.130 --> 00:16:59.070
Together?

00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:04.420
Yeah.  If we form a team and battle, 
you're no longer battling solo.

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:08.810
You must duel in a winning 
manner for the team.

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:11.080
Duel in a winning manner...

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:14.320
Yeah.  That's what a team is for.

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:20.790
Since I have a team and 
teammates, I can't give up.

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:22.710
I will focus on winning!

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:27.950
No matter how hard you try, 
Team Unicorn is going to win!

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:31.190
I'll teach you how to fight in a team battle!

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:32.170
Here I go!

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:34.820
Duel!

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:36.280
My turn!

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:40.230
I summon Trident Warrior!

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:52.920
When this card is summoned, I can Special 
Summon a Level 3 monster in my hand to my field!

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:55.650
I Special Summon Delta Flyer!

00:17:58.850 --> 00:18:01.650
I activate Delta Flyer's effect!

00:18:01.650 --> 00:18:07.200
Once per turn, a different monster 
on my field gains 1 Level!

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:10.770
Trident Warrior becomes Level 5.

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:15.480
Level 3 Delta Flyer tunes 
Level 5 Trident Warrior!

00:18:16.770 --> 00:18:22.670
Hammer of the heavens, break through the black 
atmosphere and use your lightning to burn the land!

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:24.640
Synchro Summon!

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:27.840
Shine, Lightning Tricorn!

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:29.050
Is it coming?

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:32.990
Lightning Tricorn attacks Junk Destroyer!

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:34.250
No way!

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:37.190
He immediately Synchro Summoned and attacked!

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:38.470
Yusei!

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:40.940
Please do something!

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:43.710
I activate Shield Warrior's 
effect from my graveyard!

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:49.260
By removing Shield Warrior from play, I 
prevent my monster from being destroyed in battle.

00:18:49.360 --> 00:18:51.480
But you still take damage!

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:58.940
The card that your teammate sent to 
the graveyard allowed me to survive!

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:00.430
Oh really?

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:01.330
What?

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:06.160
Do you really think that I have 
no Speed Spells in my hand?

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:08.760
Speed World 2's effect.

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:15.910
By removing 4 Speed Counters, you take 800 
points of damage for every Speed Spell in my hand!

00:19:16.410 --> 00:19:19.510
This is bad!  If he takes this...

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:21.980
Yusei will run out of life points!

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:24.670
Take this, Yusei!

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:27.740
I activate Damage Eater's 
effect from my graveyard!

00:19:30.470 --> 00:19:34.720
By removing Damage Eater in my graveyard 
and a card in my hand from play...

00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:39.250
I negate the effect damage and 
regain that amount in life points!

00:19:42.560 --> 00:19:46.540
He cleverly used monsters whose 
effects activate from the graveyard.

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:51.010
Everyone knows that Yusei has 
battled in numerous situations.

00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:54.010
It's natural that he would do that.

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:54.980
I end my turn!

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:56.450
My turn!

00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:00.400
I activate Speed World 2's effect!

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:05.040
By removing 10 Speed Counters, 
I destroy Lightning Tricorn!

00:20:05.960 --> 00:20:08.590
Junk Destroyer attacks you directly!

00:20:08.590 --> 00:20:09.870
Destroy Knuckle!

00:20:11.050 --> 00:20:13.610
The trap card Reanimation Wave!

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:21.500
When a Synchro Monster attacks me 
directly, the battle damage is halved!

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:24.230
I Special Summon a Synchro 
Monster from my graveyard

00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:27.920
whose Level is equal to the 
attacking Synchro Monster!

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:30.970
Resurrect, Lightning Tricorn!

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:33.970
I summon Sonic Chick in defense position!

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:41.680
A monster with 1900-or-more attack 
points can't destroy it in battle.

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:42.620
I end my turn!

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:45.060
He has three cards left in his deck!

00:20:45.290 --> 00:20:47.330
At this rate, he won't survive!

00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:50.810
My turn!

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:54.110
I summon Rhinotaurus!

00:20:57.160 --> 00:21:00.880
Lightning Tricorn attacks Junk Destroyer!

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:08.990
I'm not done, Yusei!

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:11.720
Rhinotaurus attacks Sonic Chick!

00:21:17.930 --> 00:21:19.740
He managed to survive.

00:21:19.740 --> 00:21:22.390
But Yusei lost life points!

00:21:22.390 --> 00:21:24.400
I'm not done!

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:27.250
When at least two of your 
monsters are destroyed

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:31.540
in battle this turn, 
Rhinotaurus can attack again!

00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:32.660
What?

00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:35.140
This will finish you, Yusei Fudo!

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:38.620
Rhinotaurus attacks you directly!

00:21:39.930 --> 00:21:40.600
This is bad!

00:21:40.600 --> 00:21:41.570
Yusei!

00:22:08.270 --> 00:22:12.940
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:17.950
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:18.220 --> 00:22:22.850
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:22.850 --> 00:22:27.860
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:28.060 --> 00:22:32.730
The cruel god tests us

00:22:33.030 --> 00:22:39.670
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:39.670 --> 00:22:43.510
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:43.510 --> 00:22:49.380
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:49.550 --> 00:22:53.280
Bond is the proper word

00:22:53.280 --> 00:22:59.220
As we fight, we understand each other

00:22:59.220 --> 00:23:02.190
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:04.430
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:04.430 --> 00:23:09.100
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:11.970
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:11.970 --> 00:23:15.440
You want to party until the morning

00:23:15.440 --> 00:23:18.680
At our special place
